# AI Notes — environment variables
#
# Scope every one of these to PRODUCTION ONLY in the Vercel dashboard, or
# password-protect preview deployments. A preview URL otherwise runs the same
# code against the same keys, on a hostname nobody is watching.
#
# Confirm the repo is private and .env is gitignored BEFORE creating any key.

# --- Auth ---------------------------------------------------------------
# A passphrase, not four digits. The throttle in api/auth.mjs is per warm
# instance and will not stop a determined guesser.
APP_PASSCODE=

# Signs the session cookie. Not in the original manifest — added because a
# bare boolean cookie can be forged by anyone who can type document.cookie.
# Generate with:  openssl rand -hex 32
SESSION_SECRET=

# --- Transcription ------------------------------------------------------
SPEECHMATICS_API_KEY=

# Processing region. Speechmatics decide the region by the hostname called and
# nothing else; the DPIA (§2.7) records EU1. The default is EU1, and
# api/transcribe.mjs refuses to start against any host that is not
# eu1./eu2.asr.api.speechmatics.com. Leave unset, or set exactly this:
# SPEECHMATICS_API_BASE=https://eu1.asr.api.speechmatics.com/v2

# --- Extraction ---------------------------------------------------------
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
AWS_REGION=eu-west-2

# Declares the data residency the DPIA claims, and is ENFORCED at runtime:
# api/extract.mjs refuses to sign a request whose model id or region contradicts
# it. "eu" or "uk".
#
# UK-ONLY IS NOT CURRENTLY ACHIEVABLE HERE. Bedrock does not offer single-region
# routing for Claude in eu-west-2 — London is a Global/EU region, not an
# "in-region only" one — and every current Claude model requires an inference
# profile prefix; a bare model id returns HTTP 400. Setting this to "uk" will
# therefore refuse every working configuration, deliberately, rather than let the
# footprint quietly widen. If UK-only is a hard requirement, the extraction step
# needs a different provider.
DATA_RESIDENCY=eu

# Must carry the "eu." prefix while DATA_RESIDENCY=eu. A "global." or "us."
# profile would place patient audio outside the adequacy area and is refused
# before the request is signed.
#
# NOTE ON THE FORMAT: the Claude 5 generation has no version suffix. Earlier
# models looked like anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0; Opus 5, Sonnet 5
# and Fable 5 are simply anthropic.claude-opus-5 and so on, because they carry no
# ARN-versioned model IDs. A trailing -v1:0 on one of these is wrong and will
# fail. They remain reachable through InvokeModel on bedrock-runtime, which is
# the endpoint api/extract.mjs uses.
BEDROCK_MODEL_ID=eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0

# SUFFIX RULE - this bites both ways, so read it before changing the model.
#   Claude 5 generation (Opus 5, Sonnet 5): NO version suffix.
#       eu.anthropic.claude-opus-5
#   Anything earlier (Sonnet 4.5, Haiku 4.5): FULL dated suffix, required.
#       eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0
# Getting it wrong gives "The provided model identifier is invalid", which reads
# like a typo rather than a generational naming change.
#
# To find the exact string: Bedrock console -> Model catalog -> the model. The id
# is in the page URL and in the Details table.
#
# ACCOUNT GATING, Aug 2026: eu.anthropic.claude-opus-5 and .claude-sonnet-5 were
# both refused with "not available for this account" and a pointer to AWS Sales.
# Verified in the console playground with administrator credentials, so it is not
# IAM, not signing, not the eu. prefix. Sonnet 4.5 works on the same account via
# the same EU profile. The Claude 5 generation appears to be withheld from new
# accounts pending billing history. See AWS-ACCESS.md if you want to pursue it.

# Worth testing rather than assuming. This task is structuring a transcript at
# temperature 0, and the failure mode that matters is the model being helpful and
# inventing risks nobody named. Swap this to eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5,
# redeploy, and re-run the seven fixtures in tests/. If Sonnet passes
# extraction-vague and patient-raises-risk as cleanly, it is the right choice and
# a great deal cheaper per consultation.
